171	
172	 	\ref{item:prop-four-edges-1}. If $x_1$ and $z_1$ are any pair of edges not sharing a vertex, then the group picture of Figure \ref{fig:k33-generators} establishes the twisted commutation relation. If $x_2$ and $z_2$ are any other pair of edges which do not share a vertex, then there is an automorphism of the graph $K_{3,3}$ sending $x_1\mapsto x_2$ and $z_1\mapsto z_2$. Therefore, we can draw the same group picture with a different labeling to prove that $x_2$ and $z_2$ share the same twisted commutation relation.
